From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: trace kmem claim placement

Temporary diagnostic: kmem_range_init stops with
"vm_map_locate_space failing for claim zones" on the 4K layout.  Print the
map bounds and the cursor/size for every claim so the failing one can be
identified from the framebuffer log.
---
 osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -3638,6 +3638,11 @@ kmem_range_init(void)
 	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < kmem_claim_count; i++) {
 		vm_map_offset_t end = 0;
 		struct kmem_range_startup_spec sp = kmem_claims[i];
 		struct mach_vm_range *sp_range = sp.kc_range;
+		printf("kmemdbg[%u] %s sz=%llx start=%llx max=%llx\n", i,
+		    sp.kc_name,
+		    (unsigned long long)sp.kc_size,
+		    (unsigned long long)start,
+		    (unsigned long long)kernel_map->max_offset);
 		if (vm_map_locate_space(kernel_map, sp.kc_size, 0,
 		    VM_MAP_KERNEL_FLAGS_ANYWHERE(), &start, NULL) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
 			panic("kmem_range_init: vm_map_locate_space failing for claim %s",
